<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abidjan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abidjan is the largest city and economic capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-coast">Ivory Coast</a>, on the Ébrié Lagoon. A small village chosen as a railway terminus, it became the capital of the French colony in 1934, and the opening of the Vridi canal around 1950 made it a deep-water port. It remained the capital after independence until Yamoussoukro was designated the official capital in 1983, and is one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a>'s largest cities.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abidjan.jpg" alt="Abidjan" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Abiba Pauline · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Visite_du_mus%C3%A9e_de_civilisation_de_C%C3%B4te_d%27Ivoire_08.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
